    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Pension Familiale La Seyne offers home sitting and boarding in La Seyne-sur-Mer, for all breeds and ages of dogs. According to its official Facebook page, the business would have been running for 8 years and would present itself as accredited by the Ministry of Agriculture.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>This listing relies on a single source — the facility's official Facebook page — with no second independent cross-check found to date. The 8 years of experience and the ministerial accreditation mentioned should therefore be taken as information provided by the provider itself, not as facts verified by a third-party source. If the official accreditation matters to you, ask to see the document directly before entrusting your dog.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: always ask to see proof of official accreditation (a number, a document) when a boarding facility claims one — it costs nothing to check before leaving your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Châteaubanne area, north of La Seyne-sur-Mer, gives quick access to Six-Fours-les-Plages and the Toulon coastline.</p>
